  "sectionId": "s4",
  "title": "Replay preserves experience while changing the training order",
  "introduction": "Consider three symbolic experiences of the form $e=(s,a,r,s')$. In this constructed example, $e_\\alpha$ is explicitly nonterminal, so its target includes a continuation term. The walkthrough follows $e_\\gamma$ into the persistent replay pool, selects the earlier $e_\\alpha$ uniformly without removing it, and constructs the paper's target $y_\\alpha=r_\\alpha+\\gamma\\max_{a'}Q(s'_\\alpha,a';\\theta_{i-1})$. A later draw can reuse the same stored transition.",
