    {
      "title": "The sampled error updates the Q-network",
      "explanation": "The active update compares $y_\\alpha$ with $Q(s_\\alpha,a_\\alpha;\\theta_i)$ and takes one stochastic gradient step. The alias $\\theta_{post}$ denotes the result of this illustrated step, not a new source-defined iteration index. Replay remains available, so the update consumes neither $e_\\alpha$ nor the rest of the pool.",
