    {
      "title": "A later draw can reuse the same experience",
      "explanation": "After the completed step, replay still contains $e_\\alpha$, $e_\\beta$, and $e_\\gamma$. A later uniform draw may select $e_\\alpha$ again, preserving its transition identity while starting a new Q-learning computation under the then-current parameters. The pending next-values, target, and prediction belong to that new computation; they do not erase the values already used in the preceding update. This potential reuse is the paper's data-efficiency benefit and does not imply prioritized replay.",
      "sourceIds": [
        "section-4"
      ],
