  "takeaway": "Replay preserves a shared pool of transition identities while uniform draws change the training order and permit reuse. For the explicitly nonterminal $e_\\alpha$, the selected tuple supplies both its Bellman target and the recorded pair whose current prediction is updated, without consuming the stored transition.",
